{"id": "EUVD-2026-102044", "enisaUuid": "fa34427d-d06e-352d-8f42-ed8438e9bc3f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv4: validate checksum_start before completing checksum\n\nIf a packet with bad checksum metadata gets into the ipv4 stack,\nskb_checksum_help can corrupt the network header and cause a bunch of\nmischief.\n\nThis was discovered and reported by Paulos, and has been reporoduced\nby others independently since.\n\nWe really shouldn't allow such packets in, but as a defence\nin depth measure, let's also check before we complete the checksum.\n\nA more complete validation at input is forthcoming, but needs more work.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T12:19:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T21:19:28", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a464d950f31c89565cbaae038cc60db04fe01956", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0fab003ef4698e0628060a45a48f14b43ba2a40a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/94524b7b32691de2e2ce162c04d6cbc9106e5cbf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a65f69e0f38ffbed1b128029e09097436416dc8b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/32a8b0adaa18e52aaa0b246b5ffe683075354dbb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f3e835af6226f1dd12160cbd696081e9b6155de0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3e33464746166264334641dc850a36eef7e6326", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6785011f8b16abf40b1e9d8b2e332232b3e68822", "https://pwn.ai/blog/pwnescape", "https://vercel.com/blog/findings-from-the-1-million-dollar-vercel-sandbox-challenge"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99999"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0209e4ac-b444-3504-9a6b-f3eb49412f05", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "0682b97b-2779-3212-ae41-bc573afbc57d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2edd